# Shared by backend/Dockerfile and frontend/Dockerfile — both build with
# the repo root as context (see each Dockerfile's top comment), so this one
# file governs both.

# Dependencies and build outputs — always reinstalled/rebuilt inside the
# image itself; copying host copies in would also risk leaking a
# host-specific native binary (e.g. a Linux-vs-macOS `@img/sharp-*`
# optional dependency) into a build stage that then can't use it.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.next
**/coverage
**/.nx
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# VCS and scratch — never needed inside an image, and .superpowers is task
# scratch space per this repo's own conventions.
.git
.superpowers

# Env files — MUST NEVER enter an image. Runtime config is injected at
# deploy time (Kubernetes Secret/ConfigMap via charts/backend-api,
# charts/frontend), never baked in. This excludes backend/.env,
# frontend/.env.local, and any other .env* file anywhere in the repo.
**/.env
**/.env.*

# Editor/OS cruft
.DS_Store

# Documentation, infra-as-config and CI definitions themselves — irrelevant
# to either runtime image and no reason to bust the Docker layer cache when
# only these change.
docs
infra
charts
.github
*.md
